  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Teach Me Orthopaedics</title>
      <verse-group>
        <verse-group>
          <verse-line>The tools used in patient care</verse-line>
          <verse-line>are required for fracture repair;</verse-line>
          <verse-line>the femur reamed to make room for a rod</verse-line>
          <verse-line>to fix the bone given by God.</verse-line>
        </verse-group>
        <verse-group>
          <verse-line>You see, orthopaedic care</verse-line>
          <verse-line>is much more than simple bone repairs.</verse-line>
        </verse-group>
        <verse-group>
          <verse-line>One must know not only medicine and physiology</verse-line>
          <verse-line>but also biomaterials, mechanics, and anatomy.</verse-line>
          <verse-line>Preoperative work-up requires great aptitude</verse-line>
          <verse-line>as the surgeries are of great magnitude.</verse-line>
        </verse-group>
        <verse-group>
          <verse-line>Look at Frank Jobe who used a stitch</verse-line>
          <verse-line>to resurrect Tommy John’s ability to pitch.</verse-line>
          <verse-line>The players get the fame</verse-line>
          <verse-line>but remember who helps prolong their game.</verse-line>
        </verse-group>
        <verse-group>
          <verse-line>I crave to treat a career-ending ACL tear</verse-line>
          <verse-line>and allow athletes to play without despair.</verse-line>
          <verse-line>I want to dissect along the muscle plane</verse-line>
          <verse-line>and use landmarks to keep my lane.</verse-line>
        </verse-group>
        <verse-group>
          <verse-line>Teach me orthopaedics.</verse-line>
        </verse-group>
      </verse-group>
    </sec>
